# PART 8 — RESPONSIVENESS AND PERFORMANCE

## 13. Desktop and mobile

The library must work on both computers and phones.

On desktop:
- Use a larger architectural composition.
- Display multiple shelves and environmental details.
- Use subtle parallax and hover interactions.

On mobile:
- Recompose the environment instead of simply shrinking the desktop version.
- Preserve the magical library identity.
- Make interactive objects easy to tap.
- Use clear room navigation.
- Avoid horizontal overflow.
- Keep book details readable.
- Ensure the scanner remains accessible.

### Performance requirements

- Do not render excessive animated particles.
- Avoid unnecessary React re-renders.
- Avoid heavy image assets.
- Lazy-load room-specific content where appropriate.
- Use CSS transforms for lightweight transitions where possible.
- Avoid unnecessary canvas rendering.
- Do not duplicate atmospheric background components.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- Ensure the application remains usable on lower-powered devices.

Do not sacrifice performance for visual effects.

