# FINAL CREATIVE DIRECTION

I want the final result to feel like this:

You open AniVerse Book Tracker.

Instead of seeing a conventional dashboard, you find yourself inside an enormous, mysterious library at midnight.

Moonlight streams through tall gothic windows. Ancient bookshelves reach toward the ceiling. A few books float quietly through the air. Lanterns illuminate the wooden floors. You can see doorways leading into different sections of the building.

You click a nearby bookshelf. The view smoothly moves toward it. You see its actual collection of books.

You select one. It slides out from the shelf, opens, and reveals its information.

You return to the library and enter another room. There, you find an acquisitions desk where you can search for new books and manage your Wishlist.

You enter a quiet study and open your journal.

You enter the archive office and manage backups, synchronization, and settings.

Everything feels like one connected world.

**The application should not look like a website pretending to be a library. It should feel like an actual interactive library whose objects and rooms provide access to the application's functionality.**

That is the experience I want you to build.